# Story 11: Four Input Modes (50s)
# Hook: Four modes, one terminal. Shell, Prompt, Rysh, Chat --
# Duration: 50s
# Source: story-11-four-input-modes.tape
#
# Voiceover script with timing cues.
# Format: [START --> END] narration text
# Each entry should be spoken within its time window.
# Gaps between entries are silent (viewer watches the demo).
#
# Total segments: 9

[00:00.0 --> 00:03.0]
Four modes, one terminal. Double-Escape cycles between them.

[00:03.0 --> 00:07.0]
Start rysh -- you land in shell mode with the > prompt.

[00:07.0 --> 00:14.0]
Shell mode works like any terminal. Run commands normally.

[00:14.0 --> 00:18.0]
Double-press Escape to cycle to the next mode. The prompt changes to < -- you're now in prompt mode.

[00:18.0 --> 00:28.0]
In prompt mode, type a question. The AI sees your context.

[00:28.0 --> 00:34.0]
Double-Escape again. The prompt changes to ## -- this is rysh mode for system commands.

[00:34.0 --> 00:40.0]
In rysh mode, type system commands like help.

[00:40.0 --> 00:44.0]
Double-Escape once more. The prompt changes to @ -- chat mode for extended AI conversations.

[00:44.0 --> 00:48.0]
And one more Double-Escape brings you full circle back to shell mode with the > prompt.

